  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.246,
      "end": 4.298,
      "text": "At the core of all life,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.298,
      "end": 8.596,
      "text": "the DNA double helix holds genetic information with atomic precision."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.596,
      "end": 12.894,
      "text": "The secret to its stability lies in hydrogen bonds."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.894,
      "end": 17.192,
      "text": "Adenine binds specifically to thymine via two hydrogen bonds,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.192,
      "end": 21.49,
      "text": "while cytosine pairs with guanine via three."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.49,
      "end": 25.788,
      "text": "These electrostatic forces secure the helix,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.788,
      "end": 30.086,
      "text": "yet unzip easily during cellular replication."
    },
    {
      "start": 30.086,
      "end": 34.384,
      "text": "It is a masterpiece of quantum molecular engineering."
    }
  ],
